      "path": "README.md",
      "content": "# Pixel Metronome\n\nA simple, offline pixel-art style metronome built with HTML, CSS, and plain JavaScript.\n\n## Features\n\n- BPM adjustable from 40 to 200 using +/− buttons\n- Start and Stop controls\n- Beat counter increments on each tick\n- Flashing beat light (max 3.3 Hz)\n- Keyboard accessible (Tab, Enter/Space)\n- Responsive layout (works from 360px width)\n- No external dependencies or network requests\n\n## Usage\n\nOpen `index.html` in any modern browser. Use the + and − buttons to set the desired BPM, then click Start. The beat light will flash and the counter will increment. Click Stop to halt.\n\n## Files\n\n- `index.html` – main page structure\n- `style.css` – pixel-art themed styling\n- `script.js` – metronome logic\n\n## Accessibility\n\nAll controls are labeled and keyboard navigable. Dynamic updates use `aria-live` regions. A warning is shown for photosensitive users.\n\n## License\n\nMIT",
